        "In the annals of Islamic history, few stories capture the essence of youthful devotion and the yearning for martyrdom as vividly as that of 'Umayr ibn Abi Waqqas (RA). The younger brother of the famed conqueror and Archer of Islam, Sa’d ibn Abi Waqqas (RA), 'Umayr belonged to the noble Banu Zuhrah clan of the Quraysh. Despite his tender age, his heart was saturated with the light of Iman and an unyielding desire to defend the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.",
